<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Djenné</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Djenné is a city in the inland <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-delta">Niger Delta</a> of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali">Mali</a>, famous for its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mudbrick">mud-brick</a> Great Mosque. A major centre of trade and Islamic learning, it linked the forest zone to the trans-Saharan network. It is associated with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali-empire">Mali Empire</a> and was a key commercial city of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/songhai-empire">Songhai Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/djenne.jpg" alt="Djenné" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: qiv · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Moschee_von_Djenn%C3%A9.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
